<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Uriz et al. (2003) & Aizenberg et al. (2005) sponge spicule silicatein axial symmetry, concentric biosilica lamination, Euplectella checkerboard lattice mechanics, cohesive-zone laminate bending, helical cage ridges and basalia waveguiding — Code-to-model traceability: 89/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The v3 header docstring (L1-59) lists the Pass 3 laws with their sources and the Pass 3 section banner (L668-689) states plainly that the bending model is a reduced 1D beam, not a 3D cohesive FEM. Every Pass 3 function docstring names its equation and source (cohesive law, Hillerborg, Hermite element, He-Hutchinson, Griffith, netting projection, parallel-axis, ray invariant, Gloge), and Laws 5-7 are registered in the math-KG YAML with single-range `code_locus` pins and Lean theorem names. Deductions: stale docstrings — `measure_morphoeval()` still says \"9 reference-anchored\" (L1829) though it returns 18, `self_test()` says \"8-point verification suite for Pass 2\" (L2039) though it runs 12 checks, and the section-9 banner says \"8-Check Self-Test\" (L1826) (-4); Law 4 and Law 6 state the diagonal projection with different normalisations without a cross-reference (L489 vs L1041-1104) (-3); Law 7 has `lean_theorem: null` in the math-KG YAML (-2); the He-Hutchinson zero-mismatch criterion is applied to a silica / organic interface whose elastic mismatch is large, without a comment on the Dundurs parameters (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "models/2012-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin.py L1826–L1829: Section banner '8-Check Self-Test' and measure_morphoeval docstring '9 reference-anchored' are stale (18 entries, 12 checks) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2012-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin.py#L1826-L1829>",
        "models/2012-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin.py L2038–L2039: self_test docstring 'comprehensive 8-point verification suite for Pass 2' is stale (12 checks, v3) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2012-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin.py#L2038-L2039>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Uriz et al. (2003) & Aizenberg et al. (2005) sponge spicule silicatein axial symmetry, concentric biosilica lamination, Euplectella checkerboard lattice mechanics, cohesive-zone laminate bending, helical cage ridges and basalia waveguiding — Model fidelity to source: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 content stands (exact O_h / T_d / D_3h / D_inf_h ray algebra L153-245, 3D reaction-diffusion accretion L249-370, lamellar thinning L395-459, checkerboard shear L464-508). Pass 3 adds a correctly assembled Hermite-beam FE (L750-791; parity with 48 EI / L^3 to 1e-9), a bilinear cohesive law whose integral equals G_i (L719-747), the He-Hutchinson deflection test and a Griffith delamination balance solved on the FE stiffness (L799-949), a sin^2(2 psi) netting projection with parallel-axis ovalization gain (L1041-1104) and a step-index waveguide with exact ray invariant and Bessel-zero LP cutoffs (L1112-1203), all with Lean-checked identities. Deductions: the remediation item asked for a 3D cohesive-zone FEM; what was built is a 1D single-crack beam model (-3); the Pass 2 toughness law 1 + eta N (eta = 0.32, L104) is phenomenological, fitted to the recalled table, and is contradicted ~5x by the new mechanics (1.71 vs 9.0) — the script keeps both without reconciling them (-4); the bending geometry inherits the Law-3 outer radius 5.83 um instead of the species-table 22.5 um (-2); Law 4 (cos^2 45 deg = 0.5 per strut, L489) and Law 6 (sin^2(2 psi) normalised to 1 at 45 deg) state the diagonal projection with different conventions and the 7.5x checkerboard gain rests on the arbitrary K_axial / K_bend = 26 (L106) (-2); the k_cat -> N coupling is a calibrated mass-to-layer constant rather than a mechanistic lamella-count law (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "models/2012-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin.py L395–L459: Law-3 laminate: r_core 0.75 um, h_1 0.85 um, N = 25 -> outer radius 5.83 um vs 22.5 um in the species table; eta-law 1 + 0.32 N gives 9.0 while the FE model gives 1.71 (unreconciled) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2012-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin.py#L395-L459>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-model-fidelity-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-model-fidelity-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-model-fidelity-7> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Uriz et al. (2003) & Aizenberg et al. (2005) sponge spicule silicatein axial symmetry, concentric biosilica lamination, Euplectella checkerboard lattice mechanics, cohesive-zone laminate bending, helical cage ridges and basalia waveguiding — Morphometric validation: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1828-2037) now returns 18 reference-anchored entries and the self-test checks all 12 items. Credited as genuine comparisons: W_lam / W_mono = 1.714 vs the table's 8.95 (an honest failed comparison, L1956-1965), h_25 / h_1 = 0.1311 vs Aizenberg's 0.2 / 1.5 = 0.1333 (L1986-1995), mode count 20 vs Gloge V^2 / 2 = 20.3 (L2026-2035), fused-interlayer ablation = monolith (L1966-1975). Deductions: the two headline Pass 2 correlations (r_angle = r_toughness = 1.0000, L1855-1874) are against Pass 1 recalled table values that were written onto the model laws, so they validate nothing (-6); the k_cat -> N = 25 measurement has reference 25 by calibration (L1976-1985) (-2); the ovalization-gain entry compares an exact sum with its own closed form (L2006-2015), the ray-trace entry compares with Snell's law (L2016-2025) and the FE entry with 48 EI / L^3 (L1946-1955) — numerical parity, not empirical validation (-3); the FE model under-predicts the only empirical toughness anchor by 5.2x and the Pass 2 eta-law by 5.3x, and the discrepancy is reported but not resolved (-3); the 0.1333 reference is a recalled number, unverified (-1); no comparison with measured basalia NA or mode images from Sundar 2003 / Aizenberg 2004 (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/sponge_spicule_hexactin/sponge_spicule_hexactin_reference.json L76–L88: cross_taxa table: theta_obs_deg within 0.2 deg of theta_pred_deg and toughness_ratio_obs = 1 + 0.32 N within 0.03 for every species; no per-row source <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/datasets/sponge_spicule_hexactin/sponge_spicule_hexactin_reference.json#L76-L88>",
        "models/2012-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin.py L1855–L1874: 12-species r_angle and r_toughness = 1.0000 against Pass 1 recalled theta_obs_deg / toughness_ratio_obs that sit on the model laws (self-referential) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2012-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin.py#L1855-L1874>",
        "models/2012-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin.py L1976–L1985: k_cat -> N wild type = 25 with reference 25: calibrated by construction (flagged in the entry text) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2012-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin.py#L1976-L1985>",
        "models/2012-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin.py L2006–L2025: Ovalization gain exact-sum vs closed-form identity and ray-trace vs arccos(n_clad / n_core): numerical parity checks, not specimen comparisons <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a69596cc/models/2012-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin.py#L2006-L2025>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-measurement-12-species-concentric-lamellar-fracture-toughness-correlation-g-lam-g-mono-1-eta-n>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-measurement-12-species-porifera-silicatein-inter-ray-symmetry-angle-correlation-o-h-90-t-d-109-47-d-3h-120-d-inf-h-180>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-measurement-3d-accreted-demospongiae-t-d-tetractin-calthrop-tetrahedral-inter-ray-angle-arccos-1-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-measurement-3d-accreted-hexactinellida-o-h-hexactin-orthogonal-inter-ray-angle>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-measurement-basalia-waveguide-guided-lp-mode-groups-at-550-nm-core-a-from-lamella-2-vs-gloge-v-2-2-total-mode-estimate>,
