<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-source-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Uriz et al. (2003) & Aizenberg et al. (2005) sponge spicule silicatein axial symmetry, concentric biosilica lamination, Euplectella checkerboard lattice mechanics, cohesive-zone laminate bending, helical cage ridges and basalia waveguiding — Source and data traceability: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 provenance stands: 4 dataset files SHA-256 pinned and verified fail-closed at runtime (L110-147; specimen b562...9cf3, scout fb6e...e39f, paper_citations.bib 8118...44cd). Pass 3 adds `cohesive_bending_waveguide_reference.json` in which every constant carries a `provenance` tag (`model` / `recalled` / `exact`) with the self-referential calibration and the geometry mismatch called out explicitly (L27-44, L54-56, L67-72), `pass3_citations.bib` with six new references, and a README Pass 3 section that states which values are unverified. Deductions: all six new DOIs carry `doi_verified_offline: false` (L9-14) and could not be checked during Pass 3 (-4); the Pass 3 JSON and bib are not added to the SHA-256 registry (L90-96 pins only the four Pass 2 files) (-2); sigma_f, G_s, T_max, delta_c, span / diameter, ridge geometry, n_seawater, wavelength and the optical-core lamella count are `model` / `recalled` with no measured source (-3); the 12-species table still has no per-row citation (-2); the prompt's Prog. Mol. Subcell. Biol. seed paper is not cited anywhere in the script or dataset (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
